      nrow(tab), " features pass in at least one cluster. ",
      n_spec, " (", round(100*n_spec/nrow(tab), 1), "%) are specific to a single cluster; ",
      n_all, " pass in all ", length(d$sets), ". ",
      "Note this counts one-vs-rest results, so a feature high in two of several ",
      "clusters can still pass in both \u2014 'specific' here means specific among the ",
      "clusters you selected, at these cutoffs.")),
      style="color:#7f8c8d;margin-top:8px;")
